<title>JAPAN: 'Super Dry' puts sparkle in Asahi Breweries earnings.</title>
<headline>'Super Dry' puts sparkle in Asahi Breweries earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Asahi Breweries Ltd said Tuesday that it registered record sales and profits last year, helped by robust sales of its flagship &quot;Super Dry&quot; brand beer.</p>
<p>Japan's second-ranked beer maker said that on a group basis its sales grew 11 percent to 1.21 trillion yen ($9.9 billion) and net profits rose 25 percent to 8.23 billion yen ($67.4 million). It also enjoyed a nearly 40 percent jump in current profits.</p>
<p>All these figures rose to record levels for a second consecutive year, a company spokesman said.</p>
</text>
